solidcraft-render-server

A modified build of SolidCraft v0.44.1 (https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcraft, tag v0.44.1).
Source of this build: https://github.com/jianzhichun/solidz-render-server

Changes against SolidCraft v0.44.1 (apps/solidcraft-render-server/SPIKE.md lists each one):
- new: apps/solidcraft-render-server (this program: the editing UI drawn offscreen and streamed to
  an embedding host)
- moved: the desktop app's control protocol implementation, from apps/solidcraft/src/control_server.rs
  to crates/ui-egui/src/control_protocol.rs
- changed: crates/engine (a process-wide host read-only switch, crates/engine/src/read_only.rs,
  checked in Session::execute; a folder for per-user files, recovery::set_user_dir; a switch
  that refuses problem reports, report_issue::refuse, which this program turns on)
- changed: crates/ui-egui (system fonts shared, not copied; refusals and export status in the
  interface language; a host hook for how status messages read; under a host product's name, no
  links to SolidCraft's issue tracker, documentation, updates or community; commands a host
  refuses, which this program uses to leave out the Assistant)
- changed: crates/ui-text (a host product's name in every message)
- changed: xtask/src/layers.rs (registers the new app), Cargo.lock (the new package), and the
  messages in assets/locales/pending/command-refusals-and-export-status.json

